  "step_1": "The decision reason can be applied to the decision problem. The reason focuses on the outcomes of each lottery and considers differences between outcomes as negligible, implying that it treats outcomes as categorically favorable or not. Here, Lottery A has two outcomes: +6000 EUR (favorable) and -6000 EUR (unfavorable), each with 50% probability. Lottery B has a single outcome: 0 EUR with 100% probability. The reason evaluates which lottery has a higher probability of yielding a favorable outcome. Assuming that 'favorable outcome' means a positive or gain outcome, then only +6000 EUR qualifies as favorable. Thus, Lottery A has a 50% chance of a favorable outcome, while Lottery B has 0%. Therefore, according to the reason, Lottery A should be preferred because it has a higher probability (50% vs. 0%) of a favorable outcome.",
